Enable HEVC, AC-3, DTS and WisePlay for the AVCodecKit decoders on OHOS.

Keep support optional: Chromium obtains the supported HEVC profiles from the
GPU decoder capability query rather than advertising HEVC on every device.
No software HEVC decoder is added.

AC-3 and DTS, which Chromium cannot decode itself, go to the system's
AVCodecKit audio decoders in the GPU process (media/gpu/ohos): the
"audio_decoder" mojo media service is enabled, and the renderer answers
canPlayType and MSE from the configs the GPU process reports, as Windows
and Mac do for AC-3. E-AC-3, DTS:X and DTS Express are never offered: the
system has no decoder for them.

EME com.wiseplay.drm goes to HarmonyOS DRM Kit, as Android's platform key
systems go to MediaDrm: the "cdm" mojo media service runs OhosCdm in the
GPU process next to those decoders, which decrypt with its DRM Kit session
(CdmContext::GetOhosMediaKeySession). The browser registers the key system
without capabilities and asks DRM Kit for them the first time a page wants
it (content/browser/media/key_system_support_ohos); the renderer's key
system plumbing, so far built only with library CDMs, on Windows and on
Android, is built for OHOS too and describes it with OhosKeySystemInfo.
Software security and temporary sessions only. CdmRegistry::Init(), which
asks the embedder for its CDMs, ran only with library CDMs or on Android; it
runs on OHOS too, or WisePlay is never registered.

FFmpeg's demuxer maps DTS as it maps AC-3 -- demuxed only, decoded by the
platform -- so DTS in a plain MP4 (src=) reaches the AVCodecKit decoder, not
just DTS through MSE.

Generated against runner source snapshot 37748799880, pinned Chromium
743f26418a267dd97c3c1c71d786038ae68cfc8f (154.0.8037.51).

